Description: Functions for fitting robust functional joint models for
    longitudinal scalar responses, time-to-event outcomes, and functional
    predictors. The package implements the proposed two-stage robust estimation
    framework based on robust functional principal component analysis and
    Student-t adjusted profile h-likelihood estimation. Functional predictors
    entering the longitudinal and survival submodels are first represented by
    robust functional principal component scores, reducing the influence of
    atypical curves and functional artifacts. Conditional on these robust
    scores, the joint model is fitted through an adjusted profile h-likelihood
    approach with Student-t longitudinal errors, observation-specific
    downweighting, Weibull baseline hazard, shared random effects, numerical
    quadrature for survival integrals, and reconstruction of the longitudinal
    and survival functional coefficient functions. The package also includes
    simulation tools for generating clean and contaminated functional joint
    model data.
